{"id":"word:hebrew:H281","type":"word","title":"אֲחִיָּה","subtitle":"H281 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"Achijah , the name of nine Israelites","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to אֲחִיָּה (H281) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-pr-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 24 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"אֲחִיָּה (ʼĂchîyâh) means Achijah , the name of nine Israelites First listed occurrence: 1Chr 2 25."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"אֲחִיָּה","transliteration":"ʼĂchîyâh","pronunciation":"akh-ee-yaw","strong":"H281","lemmaId":"hebrew:H281","partOfSpeech":"n-pr-m","forms":["אֲחִיָּ֣ה","אֲחִיָּֽה","וַ/אֲחִיָּ֛ה","אֲחִיָּ֑ה","אֲחִיָּ֖ה"],"morphs":[["HNp",18],["HC/Np",5],["HR/Np",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"Achijah , the name of nine Israelites","usage":"Ahiah, Ahijah.","full":"H281. Achiyyah אֲחִיָּה אֲחִיָּ֫הוּ, (always, except where other form noted), אֲחִי proper name, masculine ( brother of Yah(u) , compare Phoenician חמלך brother of Milk, & especially אחתמלך sister of Milk , where אחת must be construct since מלך is a male deity; compare Carthaginian חתמלקרת Eut 213 ). 1 a priest 1Sam 14:3 , 18 . 2 Scribe 1Kin 4:3 . 3 Prophet 1Kin 11:29-30 , 12:15 ; 14:2 , 4 ; 15:29 ; 2Chr 9:29 ; 1Kin 14:4-5 , 6 , 18 ; 2Chr 10:15 (last five אֲחִיָהוּ ). 4 father of king Baasha 1Kin 15:27 , 33 ; 21:22 ; 2Kin 9:9 . 5 grandson of Hezron 1Chr 2:25 , or perhaps proper name, feminine , mother of preceding four, compare Be. 6 son of Ehud, of Benj . 1Chr 8:7 = אֲחוֺחַ , 8:4 . 7 one of David's heroes 1Chr 11:36 . 8 a Levite, David's time 1Chr 26:20 . 9 a chief man under Nehem . Neh 10:27 . 10 a Gadite 1Chr 5:15 ( אֲחִי ). 11 a man of Asher 1Chr 7:34 ( id .)","rootNote":"or (prolonged) אֲחִיָּהוּ ; from 251 and 3050 ; brother (i.e. worshipper) of Jah;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 2 25",